{
    "background_story": "Zeke was a struggling artist, working multiple jobs to make ends meet while pursuing his passion for painting. One day, while exploring the city's underground art scene, he stumbled upon an abandoned warehouse that would become his sanctuary. The walls, once dull and grey, became his canvas as he poured his heart and soul into creating vibrant murals. Zeke's art was a reflection of his emotions, a fusion of colors and textures that seemed to pulse with life. As his work gained recognition, he began to attract a following of fans who appreciated his unique style. Zeke's art studio, dubbed 'MOSAN' (a combination of 'mosaic' and 'sanctuary'), became a haven for creatives and a testament to the power of art to transform and uplift. His story inspired others to pursue their passions, no matter how impossible they seemed.",
